      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "PRESTIGE FANTASTIC (3) is the top pick despite a plain seventh at Newcastle, with that provincial run now followed by an easier meeting assignment. He had been sent out favourite when fifth at this track before that, and the Ben Looker-Tony Ball combination adds confidence that he can produce a sharper effort. IN AND AWAY (8) has the stronger recent head-to-head line, having beaten PRESTIGE FANTASTIC here about three weeks ago, and his 1450m record includes a placing from two attempts. ARMOURY (6) charged home for fourth at this track last start after an early bump, so he brings the best closing run into the race, although his long maiden record keeps the price honest. HELL'S KITCHEN (5) was bumped at the start and laid out on debut before finishing fifth at Quirindi, and natural second-up improvement makes her a genuine place hope if she handles 1450m.",
